# Im_player

Windows C++17 media player using SDL2, libmpv, OpenGL and ImGui. Canonical application build currently targets Windows x64 / MSVC, not a Linux player binary.

## Branches and current state
- `main`: stable integration baseline, preserved at `e9b72924facd816c671c52c567c9e513a24077a4` when alpha was created.
- `alpha`: **non-production experimental engineering line**. Integrates diagnostic PR #54 and CI cache PR #58; evidence-only PR #60 is excluded. Open P1 runtime issues remain open.
- Latest exact HEAD, CI, and issue proof must be rechecked; branch name or individual historical green does not confer runtime PASS.

Read [alpha engineering index](docs/alpha/README.md), [current architecture](docs/alpha/ARCHITECTURE_CURRENT.md), [linear issue sequence](docs/alpha/ISSUE_SEQUENCE.md), and [audit/integration provenance](docs/alpha/INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md).

## Build and validation
Use [BUILDING](docs/BUILDING.md), [CI](docs/CI.md), [BRG5 runtime evidence](docs/BRG5_RUNTIME_EVIDENCE.md). Fresh Windows x64 with Visual Studio 18 (MSVC v145), CMake 4.2+ and pinned dependencies:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\bootstrap-deps.ps1
cmake --preset windows-msvc-x64
cmake --build --preset windows-msvc-x64-debug
cmake --build --preset windows-msvc-x64-release
```

Static verification: `python3 scripts/ci_sanity.py`. A passing static script is NOT a substitute for physical Windows playback/seek/resize/shutdown tests.

